<title>USA: Central Newspapers to buy back Class A shrs.</title>
<headline>Central Newspapers to buy back Class A shrs.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Newspapers Inc said Monday it had agreed to repurchase 1.18 million of its Class A common shares at $49.50 each from the beneficiaries of the estate of Enid Goodrich.</p>
<p>The $58 million transaction is expected to close by May 31, said the newspaper publishing concern.</p>
<p>Central has about 26.3 million combined Class A and equivalent Class B shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Goodrich, who died in 1996, was the wife of the late Pierre Goodrich, one of the early investors in Central Newspapers, the company said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
